---
source: core/src/security/protected_reads/moderate_tests.rs
expression: "explained.expect(\"explained\")"
---
Security level Moderate blocked writing `.git/hooks/pre-commit`: under Moderate, agent commands always run inside the sandbox, even when you approve them, and the sandbox keeps the project's .git folder (git hooks and config) read-only. To make this change, a person can run the command in their own terminal, or switch to Permissive in /security (it applies after a restart), where an approved command can run outside the sandbox.
